{"findings":[{"rule_id":"WPS-004","evidence":[{"kind":"dimension","ref":"D12","page":1,"quote":"⌀ 16 H7 (+0.018/0)"},{"kind":"title_block","ref":"surface_treatment","page":1,"quote":"I.Z.B.P. (TRIVALENT)"}],"comment":"The ⌀16 H7 hole (D12) is a tight fit but no allowance is made for the plating thickness specified in the surface treatment field; plating buildup will shrink the bore and cause assembly interference. The designer should either increase the pre-plate hole size to compensate for the coating or add a note masking the bore during plating."

,
"recommended_correction":"Increase the nominal hole size by twice the maximum plating thickness, or specify that the bore is to be masked during I.Z.B.P. plating."}]}
